  "goodToKnow": "Der Spitzenkandidat (die Spitzenkandidatin) is a party's lead candidate, at the top of its electoral list (Landesliste). In federal elections, major parties name a Kanzlerkandidat, and the leading candidates meet in TV-Duelle (debates). In EU elections, the Spitzenkandidaten system links the leading candidate to the Commission presidency. Weak noun: den Spitzenkandidaten. Plural: die Spitzenkandidaten."
